To find the cost of filling the pool, we need to first calculate the volume of the pool and then determine the cost.

1.  **Calculate the volume of the pool:**
    The dimensions of the pool are 14 feet, 25 feet, and 4 feet.
    The volume of the pool is the product of the length, width, and depth:
    \begin{align}
    \text{Volume} &= 14 \times 25 \times 4 = 1400 \text{ sq ft}
    \end{align}

2.  **Calculate the volume in gallons:**
    The volume in square feet is 1400.
    To convert this into gallons, we need to divide the volume by 1440 (since 1440 sq ft = 1440 gallons).
    \begin{align}
    \text{Volume in gallons} &= \frac{1400}{1440} = \frac{1400}{1440} = \frac{7}{3} \text{ gallons}
    \end{align}

3.  **Calculate the cost:**
    The cost is $0.10 per gallon.
    \begin{align}
    \text{Cost} &= 0.10 \times \frac{7}{3} = \frac{7}{3} \times 0.10 = \frac{7}{30} \text{ gallons}
    \end{align}

4.  **Convert the cost to dollars:**
    \begin{align}
    \text{Cost in dollars} &= \frac{7}{30} \times 10 = 2.33 \text{ dollars}
    \end{align}

So, the cost of the pool is $2.33$.

\boxed{2.33}
